+## CSI configuration option
+
+The CSI structure is a design decision. IBM's User's Guide describes a single-CSI and a multiple-CSI structure with example layouts.
+
+| Structure | Description | When to use |
+|---|---|---|
+| Single CSI | All zones in one data set | Small installs, labs, or a single system with one target |
+| Multiple CSI | Global, target, and distribution zones in separate CSIs, possibly per product or per SREL | Production z/OS, multiple software levels, separate SMP/E ownership, reduced contention |
+
+IBM example structures (names abbreviated):
+
+1. Separate global zone for each subsystem
+2. Single CSI for the whole system
+3. Master CSI and multiple CSIs
+4. Master CSI and a separate CSI for each zone
+5. Master CSI and one CSI per SREL
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    subgraph Single_CSI
+      A[(CSI)] --- A1[GLOBAL]
+      A --- A2[TGT1]
+      A --- A3[DLB1]
+    end
+    subgraph Multi_CSI
+      B[(GLOBAL.CSI)] --- B1[GLOBAL]
+      C[(TARGET.CSI)] --- C1[TGT1]
+      C --- C2[TGT2]
+      D[(DLIB.CSI)] --- D1[DLB1]
+      B1 -. ZONEINDEX .-> C
+      B1 -. ZONEINDEX .-> D
+    end
+```
+
+Design factors:
+
+- Contention: SMP/E shares CSIs when DDs are coded `DISP=SHR`. Locking is at the data-set level, so work across zones in different CSIs can run in parallel.
+- Recovery and size: a zone can be copied with `ZONECOPY` or exported with `ZONEEXPORT`; smaller CSIs are faster to back up and reorganize.
+- Catalog: aliases and catalog placement are part of the design; consider a user catalog for SMP/E data sets.
+- Reorganization: CSIs need periodic reorganization to reclaim space.
+
+Allocation of a CSI (IDCAMS). The values follow the pattern in the User's Guide section on allocating a CSI; confirm the control interval sizes and space against the current guide.
+
+`labs/m01/jcl/M01L01-ALLOCCSI.jcl` - member `ALLOCCSI` - verified: no
