+## Hands-on labs
+
+### M01-L01: Allocate the lab environment
+
+Goal: create the CSI, the SMP/E data sets, the libraries, and the three zones.
+
+Steps:
+
+1. Run the IDCAMS job `M01L01-ALLOCCSI` (shown in the CSI configuration section).
+2. Run `M01L01-ALLOCLIB` to allocate the SMP/E libraries, the product libraries (target `SXYZMAC`, `SXYZSRC`; distribution `AXYZMAC`, `AXYZSRC`), `SMPPTFIN` and the procedure library.
+3. Copy `SMPPROC` (`labs/env/proc/SMPPROC.jcl`) into `SMPE.LAB.PROCLIB`.
+4. Run the zone-definition input `M01L01-ZONES` (shown in the CSI section).
+5. Add the DDDEFs with `M01L01-DDDEFS` (full DDDEF coverage is in Modules 2 to 4):
+
+`labs/m01/jcl/M01L01-DDDEFS.jcl` - member `DDDEFS` - verified: no
+
+```jcl
+//DDDEFS   EXEC PGM=GIMSMP,REGION=0M
+//SMPOUT   DD SYSOUT=*
+//SMPRPT   DD SYSOUT=*
+//SMPLIST  DD SYSOUT=*
+//SMPCSI   DD DISP=SHR,DSN=SMPE.LAB.CSI
+//SMPCNTL  DD *
+  SET BDY(GLOBAL) .
+  UCLIN .
+  ADD DDDEF(SMPPTS)  DA(SMPE.LAB.SMPPTS)  SHR .
+  ADD DDDEF(SMPLOG)  DA(SMPE.LAB.SMPLOG)  MOD .
+  ADD DDDEF(SMPLOGA) DA(SMPE.LAB.SMPLOGA) MOD .
+  ENDUCL .
+  SET BDY(TGT1) .
+  UCLIN .
+  ADD DDDEF(SMPSCDS) DA(SMPE.LAB.SMPSCDS) SHR .
+  ADD DDDEF(SMPMTS)  DA(SMPE.LAB.SMPMTS)  SHR .
+  ADD DDDEF(SMPSTS)  DA(SMPE.LAB.SMPSTS)  SHR .
+  ADD DDDEF(SXYZMAC) DA(SMPE.LAB.SXYZMAC) SHR .
+  ADD DDDEF(SXYZSRC) DA(SMPE.LAB.SXYZSRC) SHR .
+  ENDUCL .
+  SET BDY(DLB1) .
+  UCLIN .
+  ADD DDDEF(SMPLTS)  DA(SMPE.LAB.SMPLTS)  SHR .
+  ADD DDDEF(AXYZMAC) DA(SMPE.LAB.AXYZMAC) SHR .
+  ADD DDDEF(AXYZSRC) DA(SMPE.LAB.AXYZSRC) SHR .
+  ENDUCL .
+/*
+```
+
+The SMPLOG and SMPLOGA data sets must be allocated as sequential data sets beforehand. Work-file DDDEFs (`SMPWRK1`-`SMPWRK6`, `SYSUT1`-`SYSUT4`) are also required with `UNIT(SYSDA) SPACE(...)` operands; add them as shown in the User's Guide cataloged-procedure section.
+
+Expected result: return code 0; `LIST` of each zone shows the entries.
+
+Verification:
+
+`labs/m01/uclin/M01L01-VERIFY.smpcntl` - member `VERIFY` - verified: no
+
+```text
+  SET BDY(GLOBAL) .
+  LIST GLOBALZONE .
+  SET BDY(TGT1) .
+  LIST DDDEF .
+```
+
+Troubleshooting: RC 8 with a message about an unavailable zone usually means the `ZONEINDEX` data set name does not match the CSI name.
