+### M01-L03: Install a PTF and restore it
+
+Goal: observe APPLY, RESTORE, and the role of ACCEPT.
+
+Package: upload `UA00001.mcs` to member `SMPE.LAB.SMPPTFIN(UA00001)` and point `SMPPTFIN` at it in the job you build for this lab (`SMPEJOB` generates the job body; add the DD by hand or extend the REXX).
+
+`labs/m01/mcs/UA00001.mcs` - member `UA00001` - verified: no
+
+```text
+++PTF(UA00001) .
+++VER(Z038) FMID(HXYZ110) .
+++MAC(XYZMAC1) DISTLIB(AXYZMAC) SYSLIB(SXYZMAC) .
+         MACRO
+&NAME    XYZMAC1 &P1
+&NAME    DC    CL8'&P1'
+&NAME.2  DC    CL8'PTF1'
+         MEND
+```
+
+Steps:
+
+1. RECEIVE `UA00001`, then `APPLY SELECT(UA00001)`. Browse `SMPE.LAB.SXYZMAC(XYZMAC1)`: contains the PTF text. `SMPE.LAB.AXYZMAC(XYZMAC1)` still has the function-level text.
+2. Run `RESTORE SELECT(UA00001)` in `TGT1`. Browse the target macro: it is back to the function level, taken from the distribution library.
+3. Re-APPLY, then `ACCEPT SELECT(UA00001)` in `DLB1`. Browse the distribution macro: now PTF level.
+4. Attempt `RESTORE SELECT(UA00001)` again and record the message.
+
+Expected result for step 4: RESTORE fails because the SYSMOD is already accepted. This demonstrates why ACCEPT is the point of no return.
